{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said: Let there be a raki'a, etc.</b> The meaning is that the raki'a was created by HaShem on the first day, as I explained in connection with the verse ״בְּרֵאשִׁית״ (Genesis 1:1) — that everything was created together in a single utterance, except that the work of each and every thing was not yet set in its proper order. Now Elohim said that it should take its place in the midst of the waters, and that this thing would serve to separate between waters and waters. And see the verse that follows this one (Genesis 1:7)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:53:38.997533491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}